// A status bar button that starts a chat in the right account.
//
// chat-button.py asks `claude chat account` which account a new chat would land
// in, the same resolution a click uses, so the bar cannot promise one account and
// deliver another. Left click starts a chat there, middle click picks the account
// first, right click lists past chats too, both through chat-menu.py.
//
// Merge into ~/.config/waybar/config and add "custom/chat" to a modules list.
//
// The icon is U+2733, the mark Claude Code itself prints, followed by U+FE0E.
// That variation selector asks for text presentation: without it the glyph is
// liable to come from a colour emoji font, which renders in its own colours and
// ignores the CSS below. Drop CLAUDE_CHAT_ICON entirely to show the account name
// instead of a glyph.
{
  "custom/chat": {
    "format": "{}",
    "exec": "CLAUDE_CHAT_ICON='✳︎' .../waybar/chat-button.py",
    "return-type": "json",
    "interval": 5,
    "tooltip": true,
    "on-click": "claude chat new",
    "on-click-right": ".../waybar/chat-menu.py",
    "on-click-middle": ".../waybar/chat-menu.py --new"
  }
}
